WEBVTT

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.530
Option 6.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.530
You can add your own thoughts
to this list of possible options.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:10.310
Think about the possible consequences
and the pros and cons of each idea.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.770
Your third step is to sort
through your options.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.670
This means put your list in an order
from the best idea to the worst idea.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.505
A possible sort might be first option,

00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:26.470
go to the pharmacy and buy
an over-the-counter sedative.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.510
Second option, get an appointment with an
audiologist who specializes in tinnitus.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.970
Third option, negotiate with your doctor.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.330
Your fourth step is to choose an option.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.439
That typically means the one that you view

00:00:41.479 --> 00:00:44.630
as the best idea of all
the possible options.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.603
For this example, the best
choice of all the options was

00:00:47.643 --> 00:00:51.114
to go to the pharmacy and buy
an over-the-counter sedative.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.744
Maybe you chose this option
because it is the quickest,

00:00:53.784 --> 00:00:57.370
easiest, and least expensive
option and can be done today.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.380
Your fifth step
is to evaluate your choice.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.620
Did it fix the problem?

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.420
To do this, you might ask
yourself three questions.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.320
One, what worked?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.120
Two, what did not work?

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.700
Three, do I need a new option?

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.674
In this hypothetical situation,
the answer to the first question,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:25.220
what worked, might be it
gave you same-day relief.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.653
And the answer to the second
question, what did not work,

00:01:28.693 --> 00:01:32.350
might be it is only a short-term
solution and you still want

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.080
to explore some long-term
solutions about your insomnia.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.964
And the answer to your third question,
deciding whether or not you need

00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:45.760
a new option, might be that you want
to explore some longer-term solutions.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.177
You might go back to your original list
and decide that you want to try the option

00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:54.600
of negotiating with your doctor or getting
a second opinion from a different doctor.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.870
Once you implement your new option,
evaluate whether it helps

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:02.980
you to solve your problem
of insomnia due to your tinnitus.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.560
Congratulations!

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.180
You just walked through
the problem-solving framework.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.160
There are decades of research
on this problem-solving process.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.576
Of course, it can be used for many
kinds of stressful situations,

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:19.280
not just those involving tinnitus.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.476
So, to summarize about how
to use the problem-solving

00:02:22.516 --> 00:02:25.240
framework for stress caused by tinnitus.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.756
First, take a moment and think about

00:02:27.796 --> 00:02:31.620
a tinnitus-related problem
that you want to solve.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:35.240
Remember to think about whether
the problem is changeable or not.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.657
If you think it can be solved,
then get very specific about the stress,

00:02:39.697 --> 00:02:44.740
the who, what, when, and where factors
of the stress that can be changed.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.342
Start the five-step
problem-solving process by writing

00:02:48.382 --> 00:02:51.740
down the options you have
to solve this problem.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.300
Then, think about the possible
outcomes of choosing each option.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.521
Sort your options, which means
choose your most favorite option,

00:03:00.561 --> 00:03:03.300
your second favorite option, and so forth.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.768
Finally, choose one
of the options, implement it,

00:03:06.808 --> 00:03:09.800
and evaluate how good of a choice it was.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:10.940
Did it fix the problem?

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:17.160
Think about what worked, what did not work,
and what option do you want to try next?

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.471
We will close this section about
problem-solving coping by teaching

00:03:20.511 --> 00:03:24.440
you one more stress management
technique called visualization.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:29.500
This is a strategy that you can use
any time when you are really stressed.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.579
Visualization does not require much,

00:03:31.619 --> 00:03:36.240
just a relatively quiet space where you
can close your eyes for a few minutes.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.460
This example will only
take a minute or two.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.975
Please try it once, and then
you can decide whether it would

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:46.880
be useful for you as one
of your stress management strategies.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:52.540
If you start using it, you may find things
in it that you want to change or expand.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.680
It is perfectly fine to tailor this
visualization strategy to your preferences.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.177
Note, it is advisable
that if you have tinnitus,

00:04:01.217 --> 00:04:05.460
you should play relaxing music
in the background during this exercise.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:10.920
Otherwise, you might get very distracted
by your tinnitus in a quiet environment.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.280
Now, please sit or lie comfortably.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:28.110
Close your eyes,
take in three very deep breaths,

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.994
and with each breath, take a little
longer to exhale all the air,

00:04:35.034 --> 00:04:39.280
and try to breathe in a little
more with each inhale.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:49.980
As you breathe, picture yourself
in your safe, comfortable space.

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:59.550
See, feel, and hear this place
as you continue to breathe.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.357
Now think about the stress
you are feeling,

00:05:06.397 --> 00:05:11.632
and try to give that stress a shape,
a color, and a texture,

00:05:11.672 --> 00:05:17.910
such as gray fuzz, black dots,
or however you want to imagine your stress.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:25.450
With each breath, picture the air
you inhale rushing into your lungs,

00:05:27.719 --> 00:05:31.400
picking up the stress residue.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:37.239
And as you exhale, see the air
carry the residue out of your lungs,

00:05:37.279 --> 00:05:43.520
clear out of your body, and off into
the distance until it disappears.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:51.060
Repeat these cleansing
breaths until your lungs

00:05:51.255 --> 00:05:57.580
are clear of all the stress
that you had pictured.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:09.442
Take a few more breaths, noticing
the increased capacity of your lungs,

00:06:09.482 --> 00:06:15.250
and the ease with which your chest
rises and falls as you breathe.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:27.025
Feeling relaxed, energized,
and full of good, clean oxygen,

00:06:27.065 --> 00:06:31.010
allow yourself to return
to the place your body is,

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:37.633
from the place your mind was, but bring
with you a very deep breath of good,

00:06:37.673 --> 00:06:42.160
clean oxygen from the space
you have just visited.
